<title>CANADA: Imperial Oil raises Canada oil prices.</title>
<headline>Imperial Oil raises Canada oil prices.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Imperial Oil Ltd said it raised the price it would pay for some grades of crude oil by C$3.00/cubic metre or C$0.48/barrel, effective immediately.</p>
<p>The new prices were listed as follows:</p>
<p>Edmonton light sweet C$188.00/cubic metre, or C$29.89/barrel</p>
<p>Cromer light sour C$182.00/cubic metre, or C$28.94/barrel</p>
<p>Bow River at Hardisty C$149.00/cubic metre, or C$23.69/barrel</p>
<p>Midale at Cromer C$157.00/cubic metre, or C$24.96/barrel</p>
<p>((Reuters Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
